    "is_active": false,
    "site_description": "Hawa Mahal, or the \"Palace of Winds,\" is an iconic monument in Jaipur, Rajasthan. Built in 1799 by Maharaja Sawai Pratap Singh, the palace was designed by Lal Chand Ustad in the form of Lord Krishna's crown. Its unique five-storey facade with 953 small windows, or jharokhas, allowed royal women to observe street festivals without being seen. Made of red and pink sandstone, Hawa Mahal is a stunning example of Rajput architecture and a must-visit landmark.",
    "docId": "hawa-mahal-001"
