    "is_active": false,
    "site_description": "India Gate is a prominent war memorial in New Delhi, built in honor of the soldiers of the Indian Army who lost their lives during World War I and the Third Anglo-Afghan War. Designed by Sir Edwin Lutyens and completed in 1931, the structure stands at 42 meters tall, featuring the names of over 13,000 soldiers inscribed on its surface. The eternal flame, Amar Jawan Jyoti, burns in tribute to the unknown soldiers, making it a powerful symbol of sacrifice and national pride.",
